<%- include('partials/header’) %>
        <main class="content-area">
            <div class="care-section">
                <h2>Essential Dog Care Guide</h2>

                <div class="care-topic">
                    <h3>Nutrition and Feeding</h3>
                    <p>Proper nutrition is crucial for your dog's health and happiness. Feed high-quality dog food appropriate for your pet's age, size, and activity level.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Feed twice daily on a consistent schedule</li>
                        <li>Always provide fresh, clean water</li>
                        <li>Choose age-appropriate food (puppy, adult, senior)</li>
                        <li>Monitor portion sizes to prevent obesity</li>
                        <li>Consult your vet about specific dietary needs</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="care-topic">
                    <h3>Exercise and Activity</h3>
                    <p>Regular exercise is essential for your dog's physical and mental well-being. The amount needed varies by breed, age, and health status.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Daily walks (at least 30 minutes to 2 hours, depending on breed)</li>
                        <li>Interactive play sessions</li>
                        <li>Mental stimulation through training and puzzle toys</li>
                        <li>Safe off-leash exercise in appropriate areas</li>
                        <li>Adjust exercise based on weather conditions</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="care-topic">
                    <h3>Health and Veterinary Care</h3>
                    <p>Regular veterinary care is crucial for maintaining your dog's health and preventing serious issues.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Annual check-ups and vaccinations</li>
                        <li>Regular parasite prevention (fleas, ticks, heartworm)</li>
                        <li>Dental care and teeth cleaning</li>
                        <li>Spaying or neutering</li>
                        <li>Watch for changes in behavior or appetite</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="care-topic">
                    <h3>Grooming</h3>
                    <p>Regular grooming keeps your dog clean and healthy while allowing you to check for any health issues.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Regular brushing (frequency depends on coat type)</li>
                        <li>Bathing as needed with dog-specific shampoo</li>
                        <li>Nail trimming every 4-6 weeks</li>
                        <li>Ear cleaning and dental care</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <p class="source-credit">
                    Content sourced collected from <a href="https://www.aspca.org/pet-care/dog-care/general-dog-care#:~:text=Help%20keep%20your%20dog%20clean,all%20mats%20from%20the%20coat.">aspca</a>
                    For specific medical advice, please consult with your veterinarian.
                </p>
            </div>
        </main>
